In `escape_markdown`, `version=2` selects the Markdown V2 branch. Since `entity_type` is not provided, the function uses the default `escape_chars` set `r"\_*[]()~`>#+-=|{}.!"`. The `re.sub` call then adds a backslash before every character from that set found in the input, so `_ [ ] ( ) ~ \` > # + - = | { } . !` are each escaped, and the two literal backslashes in `and slash \\ end` each become escaped as well.

## Answer
